 "turns": [
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Doctor, thank you for seeing us, I'm still shaking. Nuala swallowed a little battery, the flat round kind from the remote, and I've not slept since."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I'd be shaking too. Take a breath. She's well in herself now? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "She's grand, she's playing like nothing happened. But I need to know it's safe. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Let's go through it. When did she swallow it?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Yesterday morning. It was only yesterday."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Two days ago! I did it!"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Nuala says two days, Mum says yesterday. So somewhere between one and two days. Did she gag, cough, anything?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "She gagged a bit and went red in the face, then it settled and she was fine."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any tummy pain since?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "She was clutching her tummy last night, but it's gone now. She's been eating a full dinner and she's laughing."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Right. What does she take, Mum?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Paracetamol syrup, 5 ml, when she needs it, which hasn't been today. And the little yellow drops, for her iron, I can't remember what they're called."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "We'll find the drops on her record. Any allergies in Nuala?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "None. No allergies."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any health problems she was born with, or since?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Eczema, a bit, on her cheeks."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any operations?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "They snipped her tongue-tie when she was a week old."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And at home, is there a lot around that she could reach?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Two parents, a baby brother, and a house full of remotes. That's the problem."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Let me check her. Nuala, will you hold my torch?",
   "pause": 8.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Torch! ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Good girl. Temperature 36.7, pulse 112, breathing 24, oxygen 99 percent, weight 14.5 kilos, and height 95 centimetres.",
   "pause": 12.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Are those all right? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "All normal for her age. I'm pressing her tummy now.",
   "pause": 10.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Tickles! ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Her tummy is soft and she isn't tender anywhere."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Thank God. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And her mouth and throat look completely normal."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "She drank a whole glass of milk this morning. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "It sounds as though the battery has passed through, since she's well, eating, and the pain has gone."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "So it's out? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Most likely. But batteries are dangerous, so please keep every one locked away, and check the remotes have screwed-on lids."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "I'll do it tonight. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "If she vomits, has black stools, or any blood, go straight to the emergency department."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Straight away, yes. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I'd like to see you again in a week to check how she's doing."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "A week. Thank you, doctor, thank you so much. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Bye-bye, doctor! ~"
  }
